  "_doc": "What each older ad's recipe takes after (scripts/build_recipes.mjs writes each recipe's 'hint' from this; motion/fullad.js fullStyle leans toward it). The owner, 2026-11-18, of the library cards and the offer family drawn as recipes: \"Library card ones are not great.. I would take them as inspiration but rebuild them all\", \"Offer family needs a rebuild also\", \"they're alright at best and seem to follow their own set of rules ? things like the heros all look so simialr\". A recipe keeps its card's words and line; its look is drawn by a seed of its own (the recipe's id, hashed), leaning toward what made its card what it was: the family's idea (a glass panel, a ticket, a neon night, a checklist, a slab poster ...) and its colourway (sun, blush, cobalt ...). Each list is a lean, never a lock: with the share in 'lean' the seed draws from the list (where the option exists and the ad allows it: a glow needs a dark ground, an underlined number a plain one), otherwise from everything, so two cards of one family are two different ads. Families: the library cards' and the designer layouts' (the id's family), the offer cards' layouts (band, center, float, info, list, row, split, type, typeCenter). A fill leans the plates' and the sticker's fill (spec/full-styles.json plate_fill and sticker_fill, where the fill is one of the list's). Grounds name a kind (photo: the card's own photograph where it fits the product the seed drew, else the line's; scene; gradient; pattern; house) or one ground by its key. Colour: tone (light, vivid, dark), hue (OKLCH degrees, the family within 35), neutral (a black, white, grey or cream ground). A library card's own theme was one of the twelve dark pairs the owner called generic, so its colour leans only where its family has one; a designer layout's or an offer card's colourway is its own, and leans.",
